  "summary": "The largest Russian public cloud, formerly SberCloud. Its GPU rates are published not on a marketing page but in the tariff annex of the contract (version 260909, in force 9 September 2026), which prices whole virtual machines by the hour in roubles. The page prints each rate with and without Russian VAT; the figure here is the one with VAT, what a buyer pays. Each card shows the machine with the lowest price per GPU, often a multi-GPU one. The dollar figure uses the Bank of Russia's official rate of the day.",
  "notes": "RUB listing, VAT included as printed: the tariff annex prints each hourly rate with VAT, without VAT and the 22% VAT apart, and the with-VAT column is published (owner's decision 2026-09-28). Scope instance - whole GPU virtual machines with their own vCPU and RAM, шт./час. One quote per card, the lowest price per GPU, per node with the count read from the row's name (also the instance label). Region null: the annex names none. Names: \"H100 94 GB PCI без NVLink\" is h100-nvl, \"H100 PCI без NVLink\" h100-pcie (the 94 GB card is priced apart and dearer), \"H100 NVLink\" the neutral h100, \"A100 40Гб PCI\" a100-40; the memoryless \"A100 PCI без NVLink\" (11 rows, the cheapest A100s) is reported unmapped, not guessed",
